# Accepted Trivy findings for the CHI WebAPI image. One CVE id per line, each
# with a comment saying why it is accepted. `exp:` makes the entry lapse so the
# gate fails again and forces a fresh look.

# spring-webmvc 6.2.19: fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9 (no OSS 6.2.x fix;
# moving needs Spring Boot 4). Neither is reachable in WebAPI:
#   XsltView RCE/SSRF - WebAPI registers no XsltView or any ViewResolver.
#   SSE view-fragment stream corruption - WebAPI has no SSE or view fragments.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-02-01
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-02-01

# mssql-jdbc: false positive. The jar is 12.10.2.jre11, which Trivy itself
# lists as a fixed version; it misreads the version as plain 12.10.2.
CVE-2025-59250 exp:2027-02-01

# apt / libapt-pkg in the eclipse-temurin:21-jre base: no rebuilt base image
# yet. apt is never run in this image (no RUN steps; non-root at runtime).
# Refresh the base digest in Dockerfile.chi when Temurin publishes a fix.
CVE-2026-109518 exp:2026-12-15
